# The greeter's log, created before greetd ever starts.
#
# The greeter runs as user `greeter` and its stderr is redirected into this
# file. /var/log is root-owned, so the redirect cannot create it: the shell
# fails before cage is even exec'd, greetd sees a greeter that exited without
# creating a session, and after five tries systemd gives up with start-limit-hit
# -- a login screen that never draws, with the reason nowhere near the symptom.
#
# tmpfiles rather than a one-off mkdir in the installer: this also puts the file
# back after a /var/log cleanup, and gives log rotation somewhere to land.
f /var/log/c7greeter.log 0600 greeter greeter -
